"pro.aggregate.menu" = "Count by Value…";
"pro.aggregate.name" = "Count by value";
"pro.aggregate.blurb" = "Counts how often each value appears in a column or a key=value field, most frequent first (what sort | uniq -c does). It finishes even on a 10GB log, with the file still open. Double-click a row to filter the document down to that value. Measured: 3.40 s to count status= across a 10GB, 86,420,337-line log (M4 Max, Aug 2026).";
"pro.columnStats.menu" = "Column Stats…";
"pro.columnStats.name" = "Column stats";
"pro.columnStats.blurb" = "For every column of a CSV, TSV or NDJSON file: how many values, how many blanks, how many distinct, the smallest and largest, and the sum and average for numeric columns — all in one pass. It tells you which column is worth looking at. Measured: 4.78 s for all 30 columns of a 1.26GB, 5,816,534-row CSV in one pass (M4 Max, Aug 2026).";
"pro.timeHistogram.menu" = "Time Distribution…";
"pro.timeHistogram.name" = "Time distribution";
"pro.timeHistogram.blurb" = "Reads the timestamps in a log and shows when the volume rose. Combine it with the filter to see, say, only the errors over time. Lines without a timestamp are counted separately rather than dropped. Measured: 3.18 s over a 10GB, 67,156,671-line log (M4 Max, Aug 2026).";
"pro.crossFileSearch.menu" = "Search Across Folder…";
"pro.crossFileSearch.name" = "Search across a folder";
"pro.crossFileSearch.blurb" = "Searches every file in a folder and groups the hits by file. Click a hit to open that line. Shift-JIS and EUC-JP files are detected and read correctly. Measured: 3.14 s for one literal across a single 10GB log (M4 Max, Aug 2026) — on par with ripgrep.";
